<title>HONG KONG: China United year net loss HK$130.73 mln.</title>
<headline>China United year net loss HK$130.73 mln.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	 24.6 loss   vs 38.5 loss</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)  nil	   vs nil</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	74.34 loss  vs 55.81 gain</p>
<p>    Net			  130.73 loss vs 169.29 loss</p>
<p>    Turnover		   361.31	vs 218.45</p>
<p>    Company name	     China United Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		N/A</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	 N/A</p>
<p>NOTE - A gift packaging and property investment concern, formerly First Asia International Holdings Ltd.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional loss on disposal of investment properties, associated companies, provision against insurance claim receivable, deposits and loans made for a long term investment project, diminution in value of goodwill on consolidation of subsidiaries and deficits on revaluation of investment properties.</p>
<p>Per share result based on weighted average of 530.82 million shares vs 439.69 million.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is nil vs 1.25 H.K. cents.</p>
</text>
